+	// Out-of-band datagram interception (Vortex Arena).
+	//
+	// ENet drops any datagram that is not a valid ENet packet, which is why a Quake-style server has
+	// historically needed a SECOND socket on a nearby port to answer connectionless getinfo/rcon.
+	// ENet already has the hook that avoids that -- ENetHost::intercept, called in protocol.c before
+	// enet_protocol_handle_incoming_commands -- and Godot does not use it. This exposes it.
+	//
+	// The handler is called as f(PackedByteArray data, String ip, int port) for datagrams beginning
+	// with the four-byte 0xFFFFFFFF sentinel, and those datagrams are consumed. Everything else falls
+	// through to ENet untouched.
+	//
+	// 0xFFFFFFFF cannot collide with a real ENet packet: the first two bytes of an ENet header are
+	// peerID|flags, the flags occupy bits 14-15, and ENET_PROTOCOL_MAXIMUM_PEER_ID is 0xFFF, so bits
+	// 12-13 are always clear in a valid header while 0xFFFF requires both set.
